# Scenario 03 -- same shape as 02, but %u instead of %c.
# With use_identity_as_username, %u is the certificate CN: the CA vouches for it.
# In 02, %c was the client-id, which any client can simply claim.

# Each device may only touch the camera subtree named after its certificate CN.
# frontdoor.crt (CN=frontdoor) -> cam/frontdoor/#
# client.crt    (CN=client)    -> cam/client/#   (attacker: valid cert, empty subtree)
pattern readwrite cam/%u/#

# Monitoring (also used by the healthcheck): health topic and broker stats only.
user svc_health
topic read health/#
topic read $SYS/#

# Home Assistant: own namespace + bulb + camera events, never config.
user svc_ha
topic readwrite homeassistant/#
topic readwrite home/lab/#
topic read cam/+/events

